 # Position Based Fluids
 
+Also called: PBF, Position-Based Dynamics Fluids
 
 ## Overview
-Position Based Fluids (PBF) is a particle-based fluid simulation method that enforces incompressibility by correcting particle positions based on density constraints, allowing real-time simulation without meshing [S1, unofficial]. It differs from traditional Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) by solving for positions directly rather than pressures, which stabilizes the simulation and prevents density drift [S1, unofficial].
+Position Based Fluids (PBF) is a Lagrangian particle-based fluid simulation method that enforces incompressibility by directly correcting particle positions to satisfy density constraints [S1, unofficial][S2]. It differs from pressure-based solvers by using constraint projection within a Position-Based Dynamics framework, which stabilizes the simulation and avoids density drift [S2]. It builds on [Simulation output](15-simulation-output.md) and is distinct from [Gaussian Splashing](1387-gaussian-splashing.md) and [Smoke Advection](4639-smoke-advection.md) by decoupling simulation from rendering and operating entirely in particle space.
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Particle positions, velocities, boundary definitions, smoothing radius $h$, rest density $\rho_0$, time step $\Delta t$, and iteration counts.
-**Outputs:** Updated particle positions and velocities.
+**Inputs:** Particle positions, velocities, boundary definitions, smoothing radius $h$, rest density $\rho_0$, time step $\Delta t$, iteration counts, particle masses $m_j$, and kernel radius $r$ [S1, unofficial][S2].
+**Outputs:** Updated particle positions and velocities [S1, unofficial].
 
