+## Subtopics
+
+### [XPBD Simulation Loop](7968-xpbd-simulation-loop.md)
+A simulation method treating a dynamic system as $N$ vertices and $M$ constraints, converting variational optimization into constraint projections to minimize system energy. It serves as the underlying solver framework for PBF constraint projection steps. See [XPBD Simulation Loop](7968-xpbd-simulation-loop.md).
+
+### Surface Tension Application
+A minor variant that applies tension to minimize local surface area on detected surface particles. It begins by calculating the normal $n_i$ for surface particle $i$ as $n_i = \text{normalize}(-\nabla_{p_i} C_{i\rho})$ [S2]. Neighboring surface particles are projected onto a plane perpendicular to $n_i$ and triangularized. The area constraint $C_{iA}$ is then built to pull particles together, while distance constraints $C_{ij\_D}$ push apart particles that are too close [S2]. The Jacobians for the area constraint with respect to triangle vertices $t_1$, $t_2$, and $t_3$ are computed as:
+$\nabla_{t_1} C_{tA}(p) = \frac{(p_{t2} - p_{t1}) \times (p_{t3} - p_{t1}) \times (p_{t3} - p_{t2})}{2 \|(p_{t2} - p_{t1}) \times (p_{t3} - p_{t1})\|}$,
+$\nabla_{t_2} C_{tA}(p) = \frac{(p_{t3} - p_{t2}) \times (p_{t1} - p_{t2}) \times (p_{t1} - p_{t3})}{2 \|(p_{t3} - p_{t2}) \times (p_{t1} - p_{t2})\|}$,
+$\nabla_{t_3} C_{tA}(p) = \frac{(p_{t1} - p_{t3}) \times (p_{t2} - p_{t3}) \times (p_{t2} - p_{t1})}{2 \|(p_{t1} - p_{t3}) \times (p_{t2} - p_{t3})\|}$ [S2].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot k)$ per iteration, where $N$ is the number of particles and $k$ is the average number of neighbors. The total time is $O(N \cdot k \cdot \text{iters})$.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for particle data structures.
